From 321f7d9fe1985535c32676b94fce70688a534d2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Henrique <150966678+zyypj@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 02:15:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add packet decode diagnostics, plugin message validation and
 misc fixes.

Bad packet reports now carry the decoding context instead of a bare id:
Protocol#createPacket includes the id in decimal and hex, the valid range,
the protocol phase, direction, protocol version and forge support, and
HandlerBoss appends the connection state (remote address, decode/encode
phase, decode direction, negotiated version, handler and closing flag) to
the corrupted frame, bad packet and overflow warnings.

Also included:
 - PluginMessageChecks validates serverbound plugin messages in
   InitialHandler and UpstreamBridge, and centralises REGISTER/UNREGISTER
   channel parsing with the configured limits.
 - PacketLimiter switched to a nanotime token bucket so bursts are smoothed
   instead of being counted against a fixed wall clock second.
 - Ping packets over the packet limit now get the kick message on
   InitialHandler, and PROXY protocol address updates go through the
   connection throttle.
 - Fixed the modern tab limiter condition, which throttled the wrong set of
   clients.
 - messages.properties is now created from a bundled messages.template,
   parsed as UTF-8 with list support, and a "shutdown" key overrides the
   restart message when present.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

